 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "O'er the new moon's golden beam,\nI've read \"The Dandy,\" etc.\nSo I went to see it again,\nAnd saw that my heart was half lucky.\nFor, as I sat sitting\nThere in the blessed sunlight,\nMy mind could not forget wherein he\nHad talked of old life and glory.\nWherein he had said again\nHow his soul hung on himself,\nAnd how a loving child lay buried\nIn the pit of some dark delirium. And",
